From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H. M. Yousuf <hmyousuf@nirapod.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:29:36 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: keep the exact bounds of an unsigned right shift

The checker abstracts x = y >> k as y / 2^k and keeps a rounding
interval, so it can prove neither 2^k x <= y nor y <= 2^k x + 2^k - 1.
For a constant 0 <= k <= w, a destination of the shift's width and a
shifted expression of that width, the change meets the exact bounds
2^k x <= y <= 2^k x + 2^k - 1 after the assignment. They hold in every
concrete state, so the change only adds constraints: it removes false
alarms and never removes a true one. The shifted expression is copied
into a fresh variable first, so a variable shifted by itself (n >>= 6)
keeps its old value, and the copy is forgotten after the bounds are met.

The tests cover a true relation that the checker now proves, a false one
that stays reported, a narrower destination that gets no bounds, and a
truncating cast that must not get them.

(cherry picked from commit d125f312e74712194769a917fc2409abf4409da6)
